cff-version: 1.2.0
title: AIFloats.jl
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
abstract: >-
  Julia implementation of the small binary floating-point formats for machine
  learning described by the IEEE Working Group P3109 Interim Report on
  Arithmetic Formats for Machine Learning: the format layer, datums and the
  code-point codec, the projection engine (every rounding and saturation mode),
  the draft's operation register evaluated to correct rounding, array kernels
  and memoized tables, shared-scale blocks, packed storage, and a live
  conformance declaration.
authors:
  - given-names: Jeffrey
    family-names: Sarnoff
    email: jeffrey.sarnoff@ieee.org
repository-code: "https://github.com/JeffreySarnoff/AIFloats.jl"
url: "https://JeffreySarnoff.github.io/AIFloats.jl"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
keywords:
  - julia
  - floating-point
  - machine-learning
  - IEEE-P3109
  - low-precision-arithmetic
references:
  - type: report
    title: >-
      IEEE Working Group P3109 Interim Report on Arithmetic Formats for Machine
      Learning
    version: 4.0.3
    date-released: "2026-09-01"
    url: "https://github.com/P3109/Public/blob/main/IEEE%20P3109%20Interim%20Report.pdf"
    notes: >-
      Unapproved draft. Its cover states that it must not be used for
      conformance or compliance purposes. This is the normative source AIFloats.jl
      is measured against; see draft_identity() for the PDF digest recorded by
      this release.
    authors:
      - name: IEEE Working Group P3109
